title The seed gets a cadence
prompt Keaton named the every-fifth-round seed push twice, then asked to gather the new Gauge documents into SOURCE.md and the README's reading list, and to make sure chronological stamping and the date path format are seated as rules or amended where rules exist.
think Wrote the foundation around the measurement rather than the intention. The seed carried 867 links naming rooms it leaves behind, 19 in the front door, and none of it read wrong from inside the field because the field holds every room. A projection published rarely drifts, and the drift hides in the one place anyone looks.
think Chose five to match the council rota rather than picking a number. The rota reads one row of its grid per lap and returns to its start every fifth, so the seed ships on the lap the cycle closes and one count serves both. A cadence that needs its own counter is a cadence that gets forgotten.
think Gave the number its falsifier, because the guide I wrote this morning asks every projection to carry one. A seed reader finding a front-door claim the field corrected more than five rounds earlier would show five too slow; a push landing with nothing changed would show it too fast and move the count to rounds that touched shipped paths.
think Checked for an existing stamping rule before writing a new one, and found stamp-and-name.md already carrying the law. Amended it with a One shape, every room section rather than seating a second rule that would drift from the first.
obs Seated the cadence in three places so it happens rather than is believed: a section in the loop seed, both prompts in the season recipe, and a block in ITINERARY. The foundation explains it; those three make it run.
obs Named what the cadence does NOT license, in the foundation and in the loop text alike -- reds still come first, a gate wanting a hand stays where it is, and sow_witness proves IDENT_CLEAN and NO_PERSONAL before anything crosses. A cadence is a floor on frequency rather than a ceiling on care.
obs SOURCE.md opens with the five reads now, and the README points at it plus the whole docs-geode shelf. Both measured after: README 13%, SOURCE 22%, door roster still gating at zero.
loom cadence rounds=5 seed_dead_at_seating=867 front_door_dead=19 gates=4 foundation_negation=18pct readme=13pct source=22pct
file foundations/20260823-111029_the-seed-that-ships-every-fifth-round.md the cadence, its four gates, and what would show five is wrong
file recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md a section seating the cadence beside the rota it counts with
file tools/launch-claude-season.rish both loop prompts carry the push
file construction/ITINERARY.md the cadence block, above the order
file .claude/rules/stamp-and-name.md amended -- one filing shape in every room, and the projection versioned the same way
file SOURCE.md the five reads that carry the whole spirit
recommend keep-going -- the seed force-push is next and it is now the cadence's own first firing, then the loop restart. Everything the push needs is green: the front door reads whole in both repositories, the field is private, and the four gates stand.
